feedback: "The literal deployment criterion remains false: live is the 9c457a3 build, not 74d60da. The worker accurately discloses this and completed T014 already proves the intended successor release; it cannot be graded as literal 74d60da equality.; Small required correction, owned by the orchestrator: update T001 acceptance/dispatch to explicitly apply the completed T014 replacement target, or explicitly scope the 74d60da criterion to its historical observation window, then re-grade using the retained evidence. Do not roll back successor releases or duplicate T014. This verifier left GOAL.md and queue.json untouched; no separate corrective session is necessary for this metadata-only correction.; All other criteria pass. Fresh historical/current typecheck, lint and unit runs passed (2299/2380 passing cases respectively; inherited 2 expected failures and 11 skips each). Current build, both 289-test browser runs without retries, 96 Forge tests, Deno/ABI drift checks, legacy live checks, phased live paths and Forge scroll probes passed. No product regression was reproduced.; Prior failure evidence remains intact. The historical StageLayout timeout did not recur in either fresh full unit run; these passes do not establish unconditional reliability under every load. Fresh production comparisons kept bytes/configuration keys in memory and recorded only hashes and sizes."
